On Mon, Mar 18, 2013 at 1:25 PM, la gleki <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>wrote:

> I'm not discovering something new. It's rather a banality. And you can say
> it's just a small note about lojban. A small note but a big problem imo.
>
> The biggest problem of this language is that it has not less than 4
> independent lists of words.
>

No, it's only part of the biggest problem with the language, which is lack
of internal consistency.

stevo

>
> Let's take {zgana} for example.
>
> gismu: zgana
> short rafsi: zga
> attitudinal: za'a
> BAI-cmavo: ga'a
>
> In some cases there can be more than one short cmavo.
> The result is that many people who wish to learn this awesome language
>  are stuck at the level of memorizing those independent, *phonologically underivable
> from each other *sets of words.
> It could have been done another way (see gua\spi) but it's a pity that
> this is a drawback of the most complete and (still !) most popular loglang
> on the planet.
